          %h3#vanishing_of_the_vacuum_amplitude_and_supersymmetry Vanishing of the vacuum amplitude and supersymmetry
          %p
            In the presence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            1-loop vacuum amplitudes are typically supposed to vanish.
          %p
            For the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Palti"} Palti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+superstring"} heterotic superstring
            see e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Han89"} Han 89
          %p
            In view of the
            %a{:href => "#OneLoopContributionAndZetaFunction"} above
            relation of 1-loop vacuum amplitudes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+values+of+L-functions"} special values of L-functions
            such vanishing reminds one of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+hypothesis"} Riemann hypothesis
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ACER11"} ACER 11
